# Uncle Mario - Guided First-Shift Tutorial (Hands-On, Punchy, Witty Fake-Skip)
# On-screen HelperPrompt shows exact keybinds while Uncle Mario speaks in warm, brisk Tito voice.
# Covers: Pricing (Alt/L), First Sale (Anoba), Fridge, Nokia Call, Store Upgrades (U), Events & Calendar (C).

UncleMario: Hoho! Good morning, 'nak! Ready to start your first day as a [i]tindero[/i]?
- Still don't know if this is the right decision, Uncle.
	UncleMario: Ha! Is that so? Don't worry, people here in Karimlan are a friendly bunch!
	UncleMario: They may look different than the city folks you're used to, but I'm sure they'll be your friends in no time.
- I'm just worried the neighbors wouldn't like me.
	UncleMario: Ha! Is that so? Don't worry, people here in Karimlan are a friendly bunch!
	UncleMario: They may look different than the city folks you're used to, but I'm sure they'll be your friends in no time.
UncleMario: Anyway, want me to walk you through a few things around here? I'll teach you how to be as fast as your Lola once was!
- Show me the ropes, Uncle.
	UncleMario: Hoho! Sige, hands-on is fastest!
- I've got this, Uncle!
	UncleMario: Hoho! Nice try, anak! But your Lola wouldn't approve of a lazy, mediocre tindero!
	UncleMario: Relax, it'll take less than a minute!

UncleMario: First, check the shelf on your left first. It's where your items live. 
UncleMario: See all those items? Let's edit all their prices!
UncleMario: How about you try with the [color=#0f6e2f]Anoba[/color]?
[signal arg="wait_for_price_change"]
UncleMario: Sharp! Remember, lower prices earn extra tips and reputation, while greedy markups earn complaints and lose reputation.
UncleMario: Price too high and they might just leave! Though... sometimes you can haggle with them! 
UncleMario: Try to find balance and switch things up from time to time, eh?
UncleMario: Speaking of [color=#0f6e2f]Anoba[/color], I'm hungry! Sell one to me.
[signal arg="wait_for_sale"]
UncleMario: Hoho! This here's my favorite snack!
UncleMario: Watch how your customers behave and jot it down in your journal, okay? 
UncleMario: Next, check Lola's refrigerator on your right. Pull the handle.
[signal arg="wait_for_fridge"]
UncleMario: [shake]Now quick! Shut the door![/shake]
UncleMario: Don't want the cold air escaping, 'nak! If you do, frozen items will get warm and have their prices reduced!
UncleMario: Now let's talk about restocking, hoho! Just call me when you need a haul, ah?
[signal arg="wait_for_tutorial_call"]
UncleMario: Hoho! Now we know the number's correct. Just be sure I'm not resting when you call, ha.
UncleMario: Also, Lola's utang notebook sits right beside that phone too, in case neighbors ask for credit.
UncleMario: Quick peek at your Store Upgrades board too, anak. That's where you grow Lola's shop.
[signal arg="wait_for_upgrades"]
UncleMario: Nice, right? New stock tiers, fridge parts, even signage posters! I haul all of it on my tricycle.
UncleMario: One last board! Check the Calendar to your right or press C so you never miss any events going on!
UncleMario: Some events are hidden, and you have to unlock certain upgrades to reveal them!
[signal arg="wait_for_events"]
UncleMario: Good eye! Active events, moon cards, and your day tracker all live right there.
jump SuccessOutro

label Satisfy
label SuccessOutro
UncleMario: That's the whole counter, anak! You're ready for real customers. 
jump Outro

label Outro
UncleMario: Tricycle's idling outside. Ring my Nokia anytime you need a haul, ha!
[signal arg="refuse_service"]
